Reduce temporary allocations while decoding MRS rules.

Source: https://github.com/MetaCubeX/mihomo/pull/3423
Pinned revision: b3c35ab197d8d21328e5f8f77847186de932d6b6

Keep the PR's production changes and regression tests unchanged. Add downstream
checks for byte-wise reads, injected I/O failures, wire-format compatibility,
buffer ownership, allocation growth, zstd frame variants and domain fuzzing.

Local comparison: Windows/amd64, Go 1.26.10, GOMAXPROCS=4; medians of three
alternating one-second runs, before -> after:

Fixture                          | B/op                 | allocs/op    | ms/op
50,000 domain rules               | 2,965,919 -> 2,034,198 | 18,883 -> 48 | 3.866 -> 2.955
10,000 IPv4 ranges + IPv6         | 2,420,010 -> 1,328,451 | 20,070 -> 41 | 6.540 -> 1.773

B/op measures total allocated bytes per decode; timings are host-specific.
The GC no longer gets a souvenir from every decoded word.

